    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "p3HiqG",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1160,
      "name": "Design notes",
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 420,
      "content": "MODEL FLAGS: one page, three tabs. Tab = whether a flag is applied; chip = what found it.\n\nAppeals (owner is waiting): the flag is applied and the owner disputes it. 1 = reject (flag stays), 2 = approve (lift). Split rulings per label when both are flagged. A hash-sourced appeal shows the shared file side by side (this model vs the seed it matched: file name, size, short SHA, identical in both). Chip \"also in Auto-flagged\" when the review window is still open; ruling in either tab settles both with the same reason.\n\nAuto-flagged (flag applied · confirm or revert): automation applied the flag. Sources: hash auto-flag (same uploader as a minor-flagged seed) and text-scan flag. Red \"flag applied\" chip in the detail header, \"N d left\" in the 30-day review window. 1 = confirm flag(s), 2 = revert flag(s); split buttons per label when two labels are flagged. Source filter: All, Hash, Text scan.\n\nNeeds review (not applied · flag or dismiss): nothing is applied; the model stays as it is until a moderator decides. Neutral \"not applied\" chip in the detail header. Sources: text-scan detection (chip \"text scan · first detection\" or \"text scan · re-detection\" after a lift) and hash match (minor only; a different uploader's byte-identical file, shown side by side; the row carries hash and minor chips, no notice). Text scan: 1 = flag as minor / real person, 2 = don't flag. Hash: 1 = flag as minor, 2 = dismiss match. Source filter: All, Text scan, Hash.\n\nCross-tab chips (amber) when a model sits in more than one tab: \"also in Appeals\", \"also in Auto-flagged\", \"also in Needs review\" (for example real person auto-flagged while a minor detection waits).\n\nDetail pane is one component with evidence blocks shown by source: Why it was flagged/detected (always), Scanned text with highlights (text scan), Shared file side by side (hash), What the owner says (appeals), Prior rulings (always), Model and Uploader facts (always).\n\nStays separate: Reports > Models, Text scan > Model rules (config), main-app Models Needing Review (publish worthiness). Header: title on the sidebar-toggle row; search (model name, id or uploader) applies itself after typing stops; no key hints. J = up, K = down in every queue. Appeals filters: All, Minor, Real person, Hash, Text scan.\n\nOld URLs redirect: /models/flag-appeals, /models/held-detections, /models/minor-hash-matches and the main-app /moderator/minor-hash-matches."
    },
